error[E0527]: a call without parentheses is only allowed at the start of a statement; write `foo(…)`
  --> 1:9
   |
  1| x = foo 1
   |         ^

error[E0527]: a call without parentheses is only allowed at the start of a statement; write `format(…)`
  --> 1:12
   |
  1| say format "%d", 1
   |            ^^^^

error[E0527]: a call without parentheses is only allowed at the start of a statement; write `mem.add_item(…)`
  --> 1:14
   |
  1| mem.add_item :sword
   |              ^^^^^^

error[E0527]: `foo -…` is ambiguous: write `foo(-…)` to pass a negative number, or `foo - …` to subtract
  --> 1:5
   |
  1| foo -1
   |     ^

error[E0527]: `foo [` is ambiguous: write `foo[…]` to index, or `foo([…])` to pass an array
  --> 1:5
   |
  1| foo [1, 2]
   |     ^

error[E0527]: put no space between `foo` and `(`; `foo (…)` means something else in Ruby
  --> 1:5
   |
  1| foo (1)
   |     ^

error[E0527]: `foo *…` is ambiguous: splat arguments are not supported, so for the operator write `foo * …`
  --> 1:5
   |
  1| foo *xs
   |     ^

error[E0521]: passing a block with `&` is not supported in Grindlang
  --> 1:5
   |
  1| foo &blk
   |     ^

error[E0527]: `a :b` reads as a call without parentheses; in `cond ? a : b`, put a space after the `:`
  --> 1:11
   |
  1| x = c ? a :b
   |           ^^
